  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "THE TIMER TEACHER\n\nA robot that trains the four\nrobots of the stopwatch, one\nafter the other, each on the\nbox in the state it works\nin -- then puts them on a\nnumber\u2019s panel.\n\nStarted: \"on\" on my switch.\nAsk: the token in hole 6.\nZero: a fresh reading, and\nwhat the number showed.\nTell: a reading and a start."
   },
   "x": -1.15,
   "z": 2.25
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "TO RUN IT\n\nGive the eleven-hole box to\nthe teacher and press Start.\n\nAsk really asks: the\ncomputer\u2019s answer lands on\nthe nest in its box. The\nothers really tell: their\nletters go to the bird on\nthe perch, and out here she\ntakes them to \u201cwhat it told\u201d.\n\nThen the number\u2019s panel\ncomes out, a box and the\nfour robots go on it, and\nit folds away."
   },
   "x": -0.45,
   "z": 2.25
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "THE STOPWATCH\n\nTake the number out of the\nteacher\u2019s box and press\nSPACE on it: it counts the\nmilliseconds from 0. \u201c.\u201d\nrests it; SPACE goes on from\nthere. Set it to 0 and start\nit, and it starts from 0.\n\nOpen its panel with the\ngear: the box and the team\nare there, and the bird on\nthe perch is a bird to the\nnumber."
   },
   "x": 0.25,
   "z": 2.25
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "HOW IT REACHES THEM\n\nA little robot the teacher\ntaught stays among its\nthings: \u201cthe first little\nrobot it taught\u201d, at its own\ndesk, with its box. Click\nthe pupil with an empty\nclaw to pick it up; click\nthe box on its desk to take\nthat.\n\nFour robots, because a robot\ncannot wait mid-round for\nan answer, and a stopwatch\nmust know when it started."
   },
   "x": 0.95,
   "z": 2.25
  }
 ],
